# Error handling

- Set `spring.mvc.problemdetails.enabled=true`. All error responses are `ProblemDetail` (RFC 9457, `application/problem+json`).
- One `@RestControllerAdvice` named `GlobalExceptionHandler` in `common.error`, extending `ResponseEntityExceptionHandler`.
- Domain exceptions extend a single `abstract class DomainException extends RuntimeException` and carry an `HttpStatus` and stable `errorCode` (e.g. `ORDER_NOT_FOUND`), added as a `ProblemDetail` property.
- Use `NotFoundException`, `ConflictException`, `ValidationException` subclasses; throw from services, never from controllers.
- Never catch `Exception` just to log and rethrow. Catch only what you can handle.
- Unhandled exceptions → 500 with a generic detail; log the stack trace once, server-side, with a correlation id. Never return stack traces or SQL messages to clients.
- `Optional` is a return type only: `repo.findById(id).orElseThrow(() -> new NotFoundException("Order", id))`.
